# {{context|fiction}} A [[government]] by [[demon]]s, be it in a spiritual or temporal sense. This can refer both to the demonic hierarchy's governance of Hell, or the spiritual governance which demons exercise over those on earth who are in their thrall. It also refers to a political system some Satanists and demonolators believe will be established at the end of the age, in which all temporal powers of governance are exercised by demons, speaking through their appointed priests and priestesses on the earth. (Akin to 'theocracy', except the priests are not of god but rather of demons.)
# {{pejorative}} [[democracy|Democracy]], used by those who believe that government by the people is no better than government by the devils of hell, or worse.



First used by me [9-11-90] to describe the agents and agencies of convening authorities of the United States government who upon notification of acts of selling, marketing, merchandizing and accessorizing "insurrection and rebellion" to the constitution and other high crimes, acts of treason; did willfully engage in murder, attempted murder, mayhem, maiming, fraud, bribery, graft, and the establishment of judicial, legislative and eexecutive selctive and constructive laundering "to pursue invariably the same object evinces a design to reduce them under absolute despotism and has instituted among man a long train of abuses and usurpations,

these agents of the alphabet gangs formed a foreign nation [hiding in plain sight] providing "aid and comfort" to a foreign nationales who engaged in terrorist acts against me for the discovery of a telecommunication technology worth about [approx.] $5 trillion [to date]; without it token ring would be the best technology could produce. 
Then in acts of cowardice maimed, injured, denied services and figuratively and literally murdered my family members. 
Whose blood lust continues to enslave free people in violation of the 9th Article of Rights "The enumeration in the Constitution, of certain rights, shall not be construed, [shall not] deny and/or [shall not] disparage others [certain rights] retained by the people.

Such has been the patient sufferance of these colonies[of slaves] whose identities have been stolen, liberties leased or rented out. --it is their right, it is their duty, to throw off such government, and to provide new guards for their future security. --governments are instituted among men, deriving their [just] powers from the consent of the governed

